{"event":{"data":{"answers_question":false,"len_chars":1631,"low_effort":false,"matches_pending_cron":false,"origin_declared":"subagent","pasted_chars":0,"turn_key":"turn-11","typed_len_est":1631},"harness":"claude_code","kind":"prompt.submit","project_key":"project-1","session_key":"session-1","source":"hook","t":1795193960402,"via":"hook"},"from":"000047","text":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a627b317dcd2e5387</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_bdrk_01WJeiV6EQWxj1Yqso6PVxZs</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-0/-home-capture-pairtime-capture-projects-cli/617e16a3-ddb4-44ca-af68-72cf58ed1a34/tasks/a627b317dcd2e5387.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Review wordcount.py\" finished</summary>\n<note>[task notification note, removed: 196 characters]</note>\n<result>I found one real bug, and the existing tests catch it. I ran them: 1 of 2 fail.\n\n1. **`count_words` miscounts (wordcount.py:6).** `text.split(\" \")` produces an empty string for every extra space, so `test_double_space` (test_wordcount.py:11) fails with 4 != 3. It also gets these wrong:\n   - `\"\"` returns 1 instead of 0.\n   - Leading or trailing spaces add extra words.\n   - Tabs and newlines don't count as separators, so `\"a\\nb\"` returns 1.\n\n   Fix: `len(text.split())`.\n\n2. **`count_lines` has no tests (wordcount.py:9-11).** The logic looks right. It skips blank and whitespace-only lines and handles `\\r\\n`. But nothing tests it, and the test file only imports `count_words`. It needs tests for empty input, a trailing newline, whitespace-only lines and CRLF line endings.\n\n3. **Missing test cases.** For `count_words`, the tests should also cover empty input, leading and trailing spaces, and tabs and newlines.\n\n4. **Minor.** Neither function has type hints or checks its input type, so passing `None` raises `AttributeError`.\n\nI didn't change any files.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>12522</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>3</tool_uses><duration_ms>139103</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
